Fix vformat() call in openxr_fb_body_tracking_extension_wrapper.cpp

The ERR_FAIL_COND_MSG path for xrLocateBodyJointsFB() passed a second
argument to vformat() without a corresponding "%s" placeholder in the
format string. Godot's String::format raises
"not all arguments converted during string formatting" the first time
xrLocateBodyJointsFB() returns a failure, and the wrapper then spams the
error every frame (~90Hz) for as long as the runtime keeps failing.

That is what fills xr/scripts logcat with stacks pointing at
openxr_fb_body_tracking_extension_wrapper.cpp:382 during OpenXR session
start-up on Quest 3 (XR_ERROR_POSE_INVALID window) and during any
transient body-tracking outage.

Adding the missing "%s" makes vformat() succeed, the error message
becomes useful ("Failed to get body joint locations: <error>"), and the
log noise stops.

diff --git a/plugin/src/main/cpp/extensions/openxr_fb_body_tracking_extension_wrapper.cpp b/plugin/src/main/cpp/extensions/openxr_fb_body_tracking_extension_wrapper.cpp
--- a/plugin/src/main/cpp/extensions/openxr_fb_body_tracking_extension_wrapper.cpp
+++ b/plugin/src/main/cpp/extensions/openxr_fb_body_tracking_extension_wrapper.cpp
@@ -379,7 +379,7 @@

 	// Read the weights
 	XrResult result = xrLocateBodyJointsFB(body_tracker, &locate_info, &locations);
-	ERR_FAIL_COND_MSG(XR_FAILED(result), vformat("Failed to get body joint locations: ", get_openxr_api()->get_error_string(result)));
+	ERR_FAIL_COND_MSG(XR_FAILED(result), vformat("Failed to get body joint locations: %s", get_openxr_api()->get_error_string(result)));

 	// Set the tracking active flag
 	xr_body_tracker->set_has_tracking_data(locations.isActive);
